Step 3 — Product & Category CRUD + Filtering + Sorting + Pagination
🎯 Objective
Create products and categories apps with models, serializers, CRUD views, filtering, sorting, and pagination.

🛠️ Steps
1. Create the apps
python manage.py startapp products
python manage.py startapp categories

2. Models (example)
categories/models.py:
class Category(models.Model):
    name = models.CharField(max_length=255)

products/models.py:
class Product(models.Model):
    name = models.CharField(max_length=255)
    price = models.DecimalField(max_digits=10, decimal_places=2)
    category = models.ForeignKey(Category, on_delete=models.CASCADE)
    created_at = models.DateTimeField(auto_now_add=True)

3. Serializers
class ProductSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
    class Meta:
        model = Product
        fields = "__all__"

4. Filtering, Sorting & Pagination
Install django-filter:
pip install django-filter

In settings.py:
REST_FRAMEWORK = {
    ...
    "DEFAULT_FILTER_BACKENDS": ["django_filters.rest_framework.DjangoFilterBackend"],
    "DEFAULT_PAGINATION_CLASS": "rest_framework.pagination.PageNumberPagination",
    "PAGE_SIZE": 10,
}

5. Views with filtering
class ProductListAPIView(ListAPIView):
    queryset = Product.objects.all()
    serializer_class = ProductSerializer
    filterset_fields = ["category"]
    ordering_fields = ["price", "created_at"]

